```{r, include = FALSE}
knitr::opts_chunk$set(
  collapse = TRUE,
  comment = "#>"
)
```

Confidence intervals for
differences of standardized regression slopes
are generated using
the `DiffBetaSandwich()` function from the `betaSandwich` package.
In this example,
we use the data set and the model used in
[betaSandwich: Example Using the BetaHC Function](example-beta-sandwich.html).

```{r}
#| message = FALSE
library(package = betaSandwich)
```

```{r}
#| echo = FALSE
if (!exists(x = "nas1982")) {
  try(
    expr = utils::data(
      "nas1982",
      package = "betaSandwich"
    ),
    silent = TRUE
  )
}
df <- nas1982
```

```{r}
#| eval = FALSE
df <- betaSandwich::nas1982
```

## Fit the regression model using the `lm()` function.

```{r}
object <- stats::lm(formula = QUALITY ~ NARTIC + PCTGRT + PCTSUPP, data = df)
```

## Estimate the standardized regression slopes and the corresponding sampling covariance matrix.

### Multivariate Normal-Theory Approach

```{r}
std_mvn <- BetaN(object = object)
```

#### Asymptotic Distribution-Free Approach

```{r}
std_adf <- BetaADF(object = object)
```

#### HC3

```{r}
std_hc3 <- BetaHC(object = object, type = "hc3")
```

## Estimate differences of standardized regression slopes and the corresponding sampling covariance matrix.

The difference between the standardized slopes of regressors $j$ and $l$ is
$\beta^{\ast}_{j} - \beta^{\ast}_{l}$.
It compares the standardized effects of the two regressors on the same scale.
The sampling variance of the difference is
$\operatorname{var} \left( \hat{\beta}^{\ast}_{j} \right) + \operatorname{var} \left( \hat{\beta}^{\ast}_{l} \right) - 2 \, \operatorname{cov} \left( \hat{\beta}^{\ast}_{j}, \hat{\beta}^{\ast}_{l} \right)$,
obtained from the sampling covariance matrix of the standardized slopes.

```{r}
mvn <- DiffBetaSandwich(object = std_mvn, alpha = 0.05)
adf <- DiffBetaSandwich(object = std_adf, alpha = 0.05)
hc3 <- DiffBetaSandwich(object = std_hc3, alpha = 0.05)
```

## Methods

### summary

Summary of the results of `DiffBetaSandwich()`.

```{r}
summary(object = mvn)
summary(object = adf)
summary(object = hc3)
```

### coef

Calculate differences of standardized regression slopes.

```{r}
stats::coef(object = mvn)
stats::coef(object = adf)
stats::coef(object = hc3)
```

### vcov

Calculate the sampling covariance matrix of differences of standardized regression slopes.

```{r}
stats::vcov(object = mvn)
stats::vcov(object = adf)
stats::vcov(object = hc3)
```

### confint

Generate confidence intervals for differences of standardized regression slopes.

```{r}
stats::confint(object = mvn, level = 0.95)
stats::confint(object = adf, level = 0.95)
stats::confint(object = hc3, level = 0.95)
```

